<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uganda–Tanzania War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uganda–Tanzania War was fought from October 1978 to June 1979 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>'s forces invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagera-salient">Kagera Salient</a> of north-western Tanzania. The Tanzanian army, joined by Ugandan exiles, drove out the invaders and advanced into Uganda, defeating Amin's army and a Libyan expeditionary force sent to support him. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a> fell on 11 April 1979, Amin fled into exile, and a new government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-lule">Yusuf Lule</a> took power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uganda-tanzania-war.jpg" alt="Uganda–Tanzania War" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en, following request by Indy beetle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battles_of_the_Uganda%E2%80%93Tanzania_War.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
